Ohle Claussen <claussen@dpi.physik.uni-goettingen.de> wrote:

>> [18]: It should be possible to gain some intrinsics by eating various
>> articles of clothing -- e.g. (as a gelatinous cube) eating an elven
>> cloak would have a chance of granting stealth. It would be
>> interesting to see intrinsic displacement... --Yui
> 
> Why not. If you can gain intrinsics from eating rings, magical armor
> seems a logical continuation of that. Be sure not to introduce too
> many new intrinsics, or the choice of armor to wear would be made
> easier and thus more boring.
> 
You could balance this up a bit by giving a chance that the new intrinsic 
displaces one or more existing intrinsics rather than just adding a new 
one. The more intrinsics you have, the more chance you have of being worse 
off when you eat that elven cloak...


